        "value": "#003087",
        "cssValue": "#003087",
        "description": "PayPal is the elder statesman of fintech rendered as a friendly, recognizable consumer-finance utility. The canvas is white, the brand is blue — specifically the deep navy PayPal Blue (`#003087`) that's been the company's identity since the original 1998 logo, paired with a lighter, more contemporary PayPal Sky (`#0070BA`) introduced in the 2014 rebrand. Where Cash App rebels and Robinhood streamlines, PayPal reassures: the design language signals 25 years of trusted money movement, not nightclub energy. The interface revolves around three things — your balance, your recent activity, and the Send/Request buttons — laid out in calm rectangular cards on a clean white canvas."
